  "cause_explanation": "The original answer fails because the available evidence contains conflicting classification outcomes for similar products (e.g., automotive steering knuckles reclassified from 7616 to 8708, transmission housings from 7616 to 8708) and unverified future policy dates (2025 tariffs). The sources do not establish a single definitive classification or rate for 'automotive aluminum castings' applicable to a specific company, instead presenting a range of outcomes dependent on specific attributes like machining and end-use. Additionally, the evidence mixes historical case studies with proposed 2025 policies, creating uncertainty about current legal",
  "confidence": "high",
  "remaining_gap": "No source explicitly links a named company to a definitive tariff classification or duty rate for automotive aluminum castings under current law; all claims are either general rules, specific historical case studies with reclassification risks, or references to future/uncertain policy changes.",
  "recovery_assessment": "no_useful_cached_support",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "passage_id": "passage_6c68e09b241d303678ae10e3",
      "supporting_excerpt": "In customs audits, misclassification of aluminum castings (70% and above) is primarily concentrated in three categories: incorrect classification of specialized parts under 7616.99, declaration as raw castings despite surface treatment, and confusion b",
      "relevance_explanation": "This passage highlights the high risk of misclassification for automotive parts, noting that finished products may be reclassified to Chapters 84 or 87, directly contradicting a simple classification under 7616.",
      "company_applicability": "national_or_sector_context",
      "temporal_status": "source_reports_effective_as_of_source_date"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "passage_810a3d7ab01abb2297486c86",
      "supporting_excerpt": "Last year, while handling customs clearance for exports to the U.S. for a die-casting factory in Ningbo, I discovered that the same model of aluminum die-cast automotive bracket was declared by different freight forwarders under HS codes 7616.99.5160 and 8708.99.81 (automotive parts), The former has a tariff rate of 2.51 TP3T, while the latter also has a rate of 2.51 TP3T but requires additional proof of the part's use in a complete vehicle",
      "relevance_explanation": "This excerpt provides a specific case where an automotive bracket was declared under two different codes (7616 vs 8708), illustrating the ambiguity and lack of a single definitive classification for automotive castings.",
      "company_applicability": "facility_location_only",
      "temporal_status": "source_reports_historical"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "passage_4fdf0756cb63480138e6db84",
      "supporting_excerpt": "Newly covered products include items in HTS Chapter 82, meaning various hand tools, saws, blades, and other steel implements now carry the extra 50% steel tariff. In addition, aluminum-containing automotive and machinery parts (such as housings, castings, or tool components) are now captured under the expanded aluminum derivative lists.",
      "relevance_explanation": "This passage discusses expanded tariffs on aluminum derivatives including castings but does not specify a single HTS code or rate for 'automotive aluminum castings' and refers to 'newly covered products' without defining the exact current status for all such items.",
      "company_applicability": "national_or_sector_context",
      "temporal_status": "source_reports_effective_as_of_source_date"
    },
    {
      "passage_id": "passage_9ab34c1af0bcef5dc8a0619e",
      "supporting_excerpt": "If a part or subassembly is sourced from China, the costs balloon further: Chinese-made automotive electronics or castings can face 54%+ tariffs under the new reciprocal tariff regime. All this drives many OEMs and suppliers to reevaluate sourcing.",
      "relevance_explanation": "This excerpt mentions potential future tariffs ('new reciprocal tariff regime') for Chinese castings, indicating that current applicability is uncertain and dependent on policies not yet fully established or verified as law.",
      "company_applicability": "national_or_sector_context",
      "temporal_status": "proposal_or_uncertain"
    }
  ]
}
